      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <!-- Card: SGPA -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] light:bg-white border border-white/[0.08] light:border-black/[0.08] space-y-2">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-brand-blue uppercase tracking-wider">SGPA</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Semester Grade Point Average</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            SGPA reflects your academic performance for an individual semester. Calculated as <em>&Sigma;(Credit &times; Grade Point) &divide; &Sigma;Credits</em> for that term on a 10-point scale.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card: CGPA -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] light:bg-white border border-white/[0.08] light:border-black/[0.08] space-y-2">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-purple-400 uppercase tracking-wider">CGPA</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Cumulative Grade Point Average</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            CGPA is the overall weighted score across all semesters completed to date. To convert AKTU CGPA to approximate percentage, use the official university formula: <em>Percentage = (CGPA &minus; 0.75) &times; 10</em>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card: PASS -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] light:bg-white border border-white/[0.08] light:border-black/[0.08] space-y-2">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider">PASS</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Fully Cleared All Subjects</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Indicates that the student has scored equal to or above the minimum qualifying cut-off in both internal and external theory and practical exams for all subjects in that semester.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card: PWG -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] light:bg-white border border-white/[0.08] light:border-black/[0.08] space-y-2">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-amber-400 uppercase tracking-wider">PWG</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Pass With Grace Marks</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Awarded when a student was short by up to a few marks (as per AKTU ordinance rules, typically up to 7 grace marks per academic year) to reach passing threshold, allowing the subject to clear.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card: PCP -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] light:bg-white border border-white/[0.08] light:border-black/[0.08] space-y-2">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-rose-400 uppercase tracking-wider">PCP</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Promoted with Carry Over Paper</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Student is promoted to the next semester or year, but has failed one or more subjects. The student must appear for the Carry Over Paper (COP back paper) examination in the upcoming semester cycle.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card: INC / UFM -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.02] light:bg-white border border-white/[0.08] light:border-black/[0.08] space-y-2">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">INC / UFM</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Incomplete / Unfair Means</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            <strong>INC</strong> means practical/internal marks were not submitted on time by the college. <strong>UFM</strong> indicates an unfair means disciplinary inquiry is active. Contact your college examination cell.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
